Cloud Foundry Runtime and Services Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and Services, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates as of 2025. The information is relevant to the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and Services' operations and maintenance.\n\n## Cloud Foundry API v2 Deprecation and Replacement\n\nThe Cloud Foundry API v2 is deprecated and replaced by the Cloud Foundry API v3. The usage of the Cloud Foundry API v2 is restricted by rate limits, which will decrease over time and eventually reach zero in the first quarter of 2026. Any direct usage of the CF API v2 must be migrated to CF API v3. [Data: Sources (873, 2537), Date_Range ((2022, 07, 14), (2026, 01, 01))]\n\n## Root Certificate Replacement in the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nSAP is switching to the \"DigiCert TLS RSA4096 Root G5\" and “DigiCert Global Root G3” PKI. The old CA \"DigiCert Global Root CA G2\" will be replaced by the newer \"DigiCert TLS RSA4096 Root G5\" (G5). Clients of applications offered by SAP and of those operated by customers must add the new CA certificate to their trust store in order to ensure a seamless transition. [Data: Sources (871, 959), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2026, 01, 01))]\n\n## Cloud Logging Enhancements\n\nCloud Logging enables loading of existing configuration during instance update via cockpit. Additionally, Cloud Logging service now supports Monitoring Security Recommendations with SAP Cloud ALM. [Data: Sources (874, 875), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Feature Flags Service Enhancements\n\nThe Feature Flags Service now supports sharing SAP Feature Flags service instances between different Cloud Foundry organizations in the same subaccount. Additionally, you can now define special properties for a particular feature flag, and add dependency flags. [Data: Sources (877, 218, 219), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 08, 21))]\n\n## Object Store Changes\n\nEven after instance is deleted, the corresponding resource will be retained for 14 days, before being permanently deleted. Additionally, AWS: S3 specific permissions for versioning and expiration rules configurations have been revoked. [Data: Sources (3677, 3678), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 10), (2025, 05, 06))]\n\n## Istio Compatibility Version Switch\n\nThe compatibility version switched from false to true, enabling retry policy for inbound routes, excluding unsafe retry on 503 from the default retry policy, and preferring DestinationRules TLS settings over metadata TLS settings. [Data: Sources (519), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 18), (2025, 05, 06))]", "# SAP Cloud Foundry and BTP Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on Cloud Foundry and BTP, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage technical risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Operational Scope\n\nThe Cloud Foundry Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating technical risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential technical pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents technical anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 10))]\n\n## BTP Governance and Compliance\n\nThe BTP Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the technical standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on security and compliance, noted starting mid-2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex technical agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technical standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (3), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 07, 10))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Cloud Foundry and BTP Departments, established in mid-2025, ensures that technical risk mitigation strategies are compliant with regulatory standards and that compliance measures consider technical risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (4, 5), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 07, 10))]", "# SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Environment Overview as of 2024-08-23\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates as of 2024-08-23. The information is relevant to the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment's operations and maintenance.\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack 1 Deprecation\n\nSAP Java Buildpack 1 has been deprecated and will be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment on June 30, 2025. This change is due to the availability of SAP Java Buildpack 2, which provides support for the latest and greatest versions of Java, Tomcat, and TomEE. Users are advised to migrate their applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2 as soon as possible. [Data: Sources (2368, 1111), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 23), (2025, 06, 30))]\n\n## SAP Digital Payments Add-On Updates\n\nThe SAP Digital Payments Add-On has been updated to support the use of pre-registered payment cards or bank accounts. Additionally, payment type icon URLs can be used in payment pages. These updates aim to enhance the payment processing experience for users. [Data: Sources (2363, 2364), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 23), (2024, 08, 23))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Enhancements\n\nSAP Document AI has been enhanced with improved machine learning models for invoice, purchase order, and payment advice. Additionally, the Document feature of the SAP Document AI basic UI has been updated with new enhancements, including improved extraction results and field selection. [Data: Sources (2365, 2366, 2367), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 23), (2024, 09, 09))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Environment Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry environment, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates as of 2025. The information is relevant to the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry environment's operations and maintenance.\n\n## SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Environment Overview\n\nThe SAP BTP Cloud Foundry environment is a critical component of the SAP BTP ecosystem, providing a platform for deploying and managing various SAP products and services. It supports multiple environments, including Cloud Foundry, ABAP, Kyma, and Neo. The environment is designed to ensure seamless integration and operational stability, with a focus on security, scalability, and reliability. [Data: Sources (1341, 1342), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 12))]\n\n## Root Certificate Replacement\n\nSAP is replacing the root certificate authority (CA) used to issue certificates on SAP domains for the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment. The old CA, DigiCert Global Root CA G2, will be replaced by the newer DigiCert TLS RSA4096 Root G5. Clients of applications offered by SAP and those operated by customers must add the new CA certificate to their trust store to ensure a seamless transition. [Data: Sources (1347, 872), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry API v2 Deprecation and Removal\n\nThe Cloud Foundry API v2 is deprecated and will be removed in the first quarter of 2026. Users must migrate any direct usage of CF API v2 to CF API v3. For information on the migration, see the Cloud Foundry API v3 documentation. [Data: Sources (195, 871), Date_Range ((2022, 07, 14), (2025, 05, 15))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of 2024. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations and development around this time.\n\n## SAP BTP Technology Components\n\nSAP BTP is comprised of various technology components, including Mobile Services, Java Server, SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime, SAP Business Application Studio, Kyma Runtime, and others. These components work together to provide a comprehensive platform for developing, deploying, and managing applications. Effective collaboration and integration among these components are essential for delivering a seamless user experience and ensuring the platform's overall performance. [Data: Sources (504, 3232), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 03, 25))]\n\n## Mobile Services Updates\n\nMobile Services, a key component of SAP BTP, has undergone several updates as of 2024. These updates include the integration of SAP Build Code, usage metering data for Build Code license plans, and the deprecation of Java Web Tomcat 8. These changes aim to enhance the platform's functionality, improve user experience, and ensure compliance with evolving market regulations. [Data: Sources (504, 3232), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 03, 25))]\n\n## Java Server Updates\n\nJava Server, another critical component of SAP BTP, has also seen significant updates as of 2024. These updates include the deprecation of Java Web Tomcat 8, the update of Java Web Tomcat 9 and Java EE 7 Web Profile TomEE 7 to Tomcat version 9.0.86, and the addition of new log fields for Gorouter. These changes aim to improve the platform's security, performance, and functionality. [Data: Sources (3233, 3234), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 03, 25))]\n\n## SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime Updates\n\nSAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime, a key component of SAP BTP, has undergone several updates as of 2024. These updates include the mirroring of Partitioned flag in cookies for sticky sessions, the addition of new log fields for Gorouter, and the update of Gorouter log fields. These changes aim to enhance the platform's functionality, improve user experience, and ensure compliance with evolving market regulations. [Data: Sources (3235, 3237), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 03, 25))]\n\n## SAP Business Application Studio Updates\n\nSAP Business Application Studio, a key component of SAP BTP, has seen significant updates as of 2024. These updates include the development experience, the addition of new runtime capabilities, and the update of the Runtime Capabilities editor. These changes aim to improve the platform's functionality, enhance user experience, and ensure compliance with evolving market regulations. [Data: Sources (1181, 1182), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 03, 25))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime, a key component of SAP BTP, has undergone several updates as of 2024. These updates include the release of the Cloud Manager module, the addition of new log fields for Gorouter, and the update of Gorouter log fields. These changes aim to enhance the platform's functionality, improve user experience, and ensure compliance with evolving market regulations. [Data: Sources (1182, 1184), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 03, 25))]\n\n## Automation Pilot Updates\n\nAutomation Pilot, a key component of SAP BTP, has seen significant updates as of 2024. These updates include the email operations catalog, the SAP AI Core catalog, and the addition of new commands associated with email operations. These changes aim to improve the platform's functionality, enhance user experience, and ensure compliance with evolving market regulations. [Data: Sources (3238, 3239), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 03, 25))]\n\n## Availability Service Updates\n\nAvailability Service, a key component of SAP BTP, has undergone several updates as of 2024. These updates include the cross-group compounds, the addition of new log fields for Gorouter, and the update of Gorouter log fields. These changes aim to enhance the platform's functionality, improve user experience, and ensure compliance with evolving market regulations. [Data: Sources (3240), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 03, 25))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry and ABAP Environment Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key components focusing on Cloud Foundry and ABAP Environment, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide a robust and scalable platform for SAP applications. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Runtime Capabilities\n\nThe Cloud Foundry Runtime in SAP BTP provides a robust and scalable platform for SAP applications. The recent addition of new runtime capabilities, such as Telemetry, Change Tracking, and Attachments, enhances the development experience for users. These capabilities are now available for full-stack projects, making it easier for developers to create and deploy SAP applications. [Data: Sources (587, 924), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 23), (2025, 03, 23))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime and Cloud Manager Module\n\nThe Kyma Runtime in SAP BTP has been enhanced with the release of the Cloud Manager module, which manages access to chosen resources and products of cloud providers. This module is now officially released as a generally available module for SAP BTP, Kyma runtime. The Cloud Manager module securely brings the offered resources, making it easier for users to manage their cloud resources. [Data: Sources (587, 924), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 20), (2025, 03, 20))]\n\n## Destination Service and Allowlisting of NAT IP Addresses\n\nThe Destination service in SAP BTP has been updated to include allowlisting of NAT IP addresses. This is relevant in situations where the Destination service makes calls to the configured target URL or to the configured token service URL. Users are required to verify if they use the Destination service in such scenarios and configure it to allow the new NAT IPs of the Destination service. [Data: Sources (587, 924), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 20), (2025, 03, 20))]\n\n## Gorouter Log Field Added\n\nA new log field has been added to Gorouter, which will be visible in application logs with source RTR: x_cf_true_client_ip. This field contains the IP address of the client that connected to the platform's load balancer. Users are not required to take any action, as the log parsing is adjusted centrally. However, users using custom parsers behind an active syslog drain may need to adjust parsing rules and regular expressions. [Data: Sources (587, 924), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 20), (2025, 03, 20))]\n\n## Harmonization of HANA Compute Units\n\nThe block size for the SAP HANA Cloud database within an SAP BTP ABAP Environment system has been standardized to 16 GB across all regions. This change eliminates the previous difference in block size between Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud Platform. Existing HANA Cloud databases on AWS have been updated to match this 16 GB block size. [Data: Sources (587, 924), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 12), (2025, 03, 20))]\n\n## Trust Configuration (New)\n\nA new trust configuration screen has been added to the SAP BTP cockpit in the global account and in the subaccount. This screen will be available together with the old trust configuration screen for two weeks before the old screen is removed. The new screen provides the same functional scope as the old screen but with a different user experience. [Data: Sources (587, 924), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 17), (2025, 03, 20))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of October 2023\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key components and their interactions, highlighting the importance of these entities in maintaining the platform's stability and functionality. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations around October 2023.\n\n## Authorization and Trust Management Service\n\nThe Authorization and Trust Management Service at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in managing access and authentication for various components. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential security threats and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security standards. Effective authorization and trust management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the platform's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (178), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 04), (2023, 10, 19))]\n\n## Cloud Management Tools and SAP BTP Cockpit\n\nThe Cloud Management Tools and SAP BTP Cockpit components ensure that all SAP BTP operations adhere to the latest standards and best practices. Their focus on providing a user-friendly interface and efficient management tools is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational efficiency, especially in managing complex cloud environments. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high standards and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (179, 182), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 19), (2023, 10, 19))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the various components of SAP BTP, established in October 2023, ensures that security and compliance measures are integrated and effective. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in aligning the platform's strategies with regulatory requirements. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in maintaining SAP BTP's integrity and operational stability. [Data: Sources (179, 182), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 19), (2023, 10, 19))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\n\nThe Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime components ensure that all SAP BTP operations on Cloud Foundry adhere to the latest standards and best practices. Their focus on providing a user-friendly interface and efficient management tools is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational efficiency, especially in managing complex cloud environments. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high standards and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (179, 183), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 19), (2023, 10, 19))]\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack\n\nThe SAP Java Buildpack component ensures that all SAP BTP operations on Cloud Foundry adhere to the latest standards and best practices. Their focus on providing a user-friendly interface and efficient management tools is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational efficiency, especially in managing complex cloud environments. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high standards and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (179, 184), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 03), (2023, 10, 19))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Management and Identity Provisioning Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key components focusing on cloud management and identity provisioning, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to manage services and identities effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Management Tools Operational Scope\n\nThe Cloud Management Tools at SAP BTP play a pivotal role in managing services and entitlements. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential service pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving service standards. Effective service management not only prevents service anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3387, 3388, 3389), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 22), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## Identity Provisioning and Governance\n\nThe Identity Provisioning Department ensures that all SAP BTP's operations adhere to the identity standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on identity governance and management, noted starting 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex identities and access control. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high identity standards and security practices. [Data: Source (3387), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 22), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Service Management\n\nCollaboration between the Cloud Management Tools and Identity Provisioning Departments, established in 2024, ensures that service management strategies are identity-aware and that compliance measures consider service risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating service management with identity compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with service standards. [Data: Sources (3387, 3388, 3389), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 22), (2024, 02, 22))]", "# Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into the key components and services of Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide a robust and scalable platform for application development and deployment. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Operational Scope\n\nCloud Foundry is a robust and scalable platform for application development and deployment. It provides a wide range of services and tools to support the entire application lifecycle, from development to deployment and management. Cloud Foundry's operational scope includes application deployment, scaling, and monitoring, as well as support for various programming languages and frameworks. Effective use of Cloud Foundry enables developers to focus on writing code rather than managing infrastructure, leading to increased productivity and faster time-to-market for applications. [Data: Sources (1281, 1282, 1283), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 03, 06))]\n\n## SAP BTP Services and Features\n\nSAP BTP provides a comprehensive set of services and features to support application development, deployment, and management. These services include cloud identity services, cloud management tools, and connectivity services, among others. SAP BTP also provides a range of features such as authentication and authorization, data quality services, and job scheduling service, among others. Effective use of SAP BTP enables developers to build and deploy secure, scalable, and reliable applications. [Data: Sources (2991, 2992, 2993), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 02), (2024, 05, 02))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP\n\nCollaboration between different departments and teams is essential for effective use of Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP. This collaboration enables developers to leverage the strengths of each department and team, leading to increased productivity and faster time-to-market for applications. Effective interdepartmental collaboration also enables the company to respond quickly to changing business needs and customer requirements. [Data: Sources (1285, 1286, 1287), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 06), (2025, 03, 06))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Environment Overview as of June 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry environment, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry environment as of June 2025.\n\n## Cloud Connector Updates\n\nThe Cloud Connector has undergone significant updates, including bug fixes and enhancements. The release of Cloud Connector version 2.18.1 provides bug fixes for issues such as the installer failure on Windows and the inability to determine whether the password should be changed for the user sccadmin. Additionally, the release introduces enhancements such as the JVM parameters NewSize, MaxNewSize, SurvivorRatio, and TargetSurvivorRatio being dropped, as the G1 garbage collector works better without those settings. The Cloud Connector now also shows the IPv6 status on the About screen. These updates are crucial for maintaining the Cloud Connector's stability and functionality. [Data: Sources (359, 657, 658), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 12), (2025, 06, 12))]\n\n## Data Quality Services Enhancements\n\nData Quality Services has undergone enhancements, including the addition of a new returnPostalCountry setting to the Address Cleanse endpoint. This setting provides control to return the country as either the territory or the postal country in the response. Additionally, improvements were made to support geocoding addresses in India that consist of more than two levels of locality and no street. These enhancements are crucial for maintaining the Data Quality Services' stability and functionality. [Data: Source (659), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 06, 12))]\n\n## Job Scheduling Service Update\n\nThe Job Scheduling Service has undergone an update, replacing the Belize UI theme with the Morning Horizon theme as the default UI theme of the Job Scheduling service dashboard. This update is crucial for maintaining the Job Scheduling Service's stability and functionality. [Data: Source (660), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 09), (2025, 06, 12))]", "# SAP BTP Platform Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into the key components and features of the SAP Business Technology Platform (SAP BTP), highlighting how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide a comprehensive platform for businesses. The information is relevant to the platform's operations as of 2025.\n\n## Cloud Management Tools and SAP BTP Cockpit\n\nThe Cloud Management Tools and SAP BTP Cockpit components of the SAP BTP play a pivotal role in managing and monitoring cloud resources. Their proactive approach helps safeguard the platform against potential security pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective cloud management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (654, 655), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 12), (2025, 06, 12))]\n\n## Authorization and Trust Management Service\n\nThe Authorization and Trust Management Service component of the SAP BTP ensures that all platform operations adhere to the security standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on improving security and compliance, noted starting 2025, is crucial in maintaining the platform's reputation and operational security, especially in managing complex security configurations and identity providers. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (358, 1350, 1278), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 12), (2025, 03, 06))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the various components of the SAP BTP, established in 2025, ensures that security measures are effective and that compliance considerations consider security risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating security with compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (9, 93, 94), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 09, 18))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of September 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their operational scope, core attributes, and connections. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's technology landscape as of September 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nThe Cloud Foundry environment at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in providing a scalable and flexible platform for deploying applications. Its core attributes include support for multiple isolation levels, improved resource management, and enhanced security features. The Cloud Foundry environment is connected to other SAP BTP components, such as the SAP BTP Cockpit, to provide a seamless user experience. [Data: Sources (665, 666), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 01), (2025, 09, 18))]\n\n## SAP BTP Cockpit Enhancements\n\nThe SAP BTP Cockpit has undergone significant enhancements, including the introduction of personalized navigation with Favorites & Recent, improved event handling, and faster page loading. These changes aim to provide a more intuitive and user-friendly experience for SAP BTP users. [Data: Sources (93, 94), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 01), (2025, 09, 18))]\n\n## Monitoring Service REST APIs\n\nThe Monitoring Service REST APIs at SAP BTP have been updated to include a rate limit for the number of requests per subaccount, ensuring that the system remains stable and secure. This change is part of SAP BTP's ongoing efforts to improve its monitoring capabilities. [Data: Sources (408), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 21), (2025, 07, 24))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technologies, highlighting their core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP's operations as of 2024.\n\n## Generative AI Hub Capabilities\n\nThe Generative AI Hub is a key component of SAP's AI strategy, enabling the creation of custom AI models and workflows. Its capabilities include data masking, model selection, and orchestration. The hub's integration with other SAP technologies, such as SAP AI Core and SAP AI Launchpad, enables seamless AI development and deployment. [Data: Sources (2275, 2276, 2277), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 16), (2024, 09, 16))]\n\n## SAP AI Core Updates\n\nSAP AI Core has undergone several updates, including the addition of new models from Meta and the introduction of data masking capabilities. These updates have enhanced the platform's ability to handle complex AI tasks and improve model accuracy. [Data: Sources (2275, 2277), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 16), (2024, 09, 16))]\n\n## SAP AI Launchpad Enhancements\n\nSAP AI Launchpad has been enhanced with the addition of new models from Meta and improved user interface. These updates have made it easier for developers to create and deploy AI models, and have improved the overall user experience. [Data: Sources (2278, 2279), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 16), (2024, 09, 16))]\n\n## SAP Cloud Application Event Hub Updates\n\nThe SAP Cloud Application Event Hub has been updated with new features, including support for SAP CAP applications as consumers of business events. This update has improved the platform's ability to handle event-driven architecture and has enhanced the overall user experience. [Data: Sources (2166), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 04), (2024, 10, 04))]\n\n## SAP Integration Advisor Updates\n\nThe SAP Integration Advisor has been updated with new features, including the ability to combine overlay MAGs with pretransformation. This update has improved the platform's ability to handle complex integration tasks and has enhanced the overall user experience. [Data: Sources (386, 387), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 27), (2025, 07, 27))]\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack Updates\n\nThe SAP Java Buildpack has been updated with new features, including the removal of DSR and the update of several components. This update has improved the platform's ability to handle complex Java development tasks and has enhanced the overall user experience. [Data: Sources (2271, 2272), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 19), (2024, 09, 19))]", "# SAP Cloud Platform Update Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and changes to the SAP Cloud Platform as of 2024, highlighting the importance of these updates in enhancing the platform's functionality and user experience.\n\n## Cloud Connector Updates\n\nThe Cloud Connector has undergone significant updates, including bug fixes, enhancements, and new features. These updates aim to improve the overall performance and user experience of the Cloud Connector, making it more efficient and reliable. [Data: Sources (1283, 1284), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 06), (2025, 03, 06))]\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack Updates\n\nThe SAP Java Buildpack has been updated to version 1.86.0, introducing several new features and improvements. These updates aim to enhance the buildpack's performance, security, and user experience, making it more efficient and reliable. [Data: Sources (660, 3621), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 25), (2024, 01, 25))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has been upgraded, introducing several new features and improvements. These updates aim to enhance the security and user experience of the service, making it more efficient and reliable. [Data: Sources (3625), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 24), (2024, 01, 24))]\n\n## Edge Integration Cell Updates\n\nThe Edge Integration Cell has undergone significant updates, including software version updates and new features. These updates aim to enhance the performance, security, and user experience of the Edge Integration Cell, making it more efficient and reliable. [Data: Sources (3626, 3627), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 23), (2024, 01, 23))]\n\n## SAP Advanced Financial Closing Updates\n\nSAP Advanced Financial Closing has undergone significant updates, including the addition of a new closing structure table. These updates aim to enhance the performance, security, and user experience of the service, making it more efficient and reliable. [Data: Sources (3630), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 22), (2024, 01, 22))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around 2025.\n\n## Connectivity Proxy Enhancements\n\nThe Connectivity Proxy at SAP has undergone significant enhancements, including the addition of a new observability metric tunnel count gauge and support for ECDSA private keys. These updates improve the proxy's performance and security, enabling more efficient data transfer and better protection against potential threats. Effective connectivity is crucial for SAP's operations, and these enhancements play a vital role in maintaining the company's integrity and operational stability. [Data: Sources (88, 89, 1028, 1029), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 17), (2025, 09, 18))]\n\n## Cloud Integration Updates\n\nSAP's Cloud Integration has seen significant updates, including the addition of a new compound evaluation type (AVG) and support for authentication using OAuth2 Authorization Code. These updates improve the integration's performance and security, enabling more efficient data transfer and better protection against potential threats. Effective cloud integration is crucial for SAP's operations, and these updates play a vital role in maintaining the company's integrity and operational stability. [Data: Sources (1025, 1026), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 17), (2025, 09, 18))]\n\n## Region Updates\n\nSAP has introduced new regions, including Europe (Frankfurt) - EU Access Only and Japan (Tokyo). These updates improve the company's global reach and enable more efficient data transfer. Effective region management is crucial for SAP's operations, and these updates play a vital role in maintaining the company's integrity and operational stability. [Data: Sources (82, 84, 86), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 11), (2025, 09, 19))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_8b1eb7e05224e662580acb7fbc220faf0727b2137e3beeabdc3eaf4b53aa6545_v2"}